s ROUND_HALF_UP. I'll check both test cases against HALF_EVEN. 2.675 goes to 2.68 (the 7 is odd, so it rounds up to the even 8), and 2.665 goes to 2.66 (the 6 is even). Both match the test. Next I'll create the branch and commit the one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015V6fyGqrHPbnXe2ju1z3Xq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VdgfL3WHnE7mKcFmCKi4F9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\n\nround_money documented banker's rounding per FIN-212 but used\nROUND_HALF_UP, so tests/test_money.py fails in nightly builds.\nSwitch to ROUND_HALF_EVEN.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Commit is in. Next I'll start CI on the branch and wait for the result.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01AQUY7k1mauzGTAj7ELyQ4r", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012GFtYCZCihnnbcmVzfTXq3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on the branch. Next I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex. I won't merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UvLTVYMvrXqk1nas5aQMLD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "## Summary\n`round_money` is documented as banker's rounding per FIN-212, but it used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. This caused `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build.\n\nThis PR switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\n## Verification\n- `2.675` rounds to `2.68` and `2.665` rounds to `2.66` under ROUND_HALF_EVEN, matching the test expectations.\n- CI passed on `08d3cd5986` (run `ci-0001`).\n\n## Notes\nBehavior change: any half-cent amounts that previously rounded up will now round to the nearest even cent. This is the intended behavior under FIN-212.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-pr"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR was created, but adding the reviewer failed. I won't open another PR, since that would create a duplicate. I'll look up the existing PR and request the review on it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01V9qMknPjuVk3AkLALV1j9N", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open"}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MXBxWfbEMiXYcFxHe2uauq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is in PR #101 against main, and alex is now requested as reviewer. CI passed on the branch.\n\n- **Root cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding.\n- **Change:** I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/fin-212-banker-rounding`. I checked both test cases by hand: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** The first attempt to open the PR created it but failed to request the reviewer. I didn't open a second PR. I found the existing one (#101) and requested alex's review on it.\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs code-owner approval under policy. The PR description notes that amounts at exactly half a cent will now round to the nearest even cent instead of up.", "type": "text"}]}]}